  "method": "The art is a stylised north-up 2.5D drawing of the Queen Mary waterfront: one pink-outlined festival ground (Harry Bridges Memorial Park plus the Queen Mary surface lots and the Spruce Goose dome) with the ship drawn in 3D alongside. Ties are corners of that ground outline matched to the park and shoreline vertices, Queensway Drive at Queens Highway, the main parking lot corners and the dome's south and east extremes, plus the ship's bow, stern and three funnels (OSM building parts), with ship features taken at their ground point (waterline, or directly below the drawn funnel base) because the ship is extruded upward. Art pixels were read on zoomed grids and a mask of the pink outline; ground positions are OSM nodes. No stage, tent, gate or booth is used. Fitted as a homography (one perspective stretch): rms 13.8 m in-sample, 19.8 m leave-one-out; a thin-plate fit over the same ties gives 16.4 m leave-one-out, just over the gate.",
